Vikram and Betal: The Lost Book (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100148

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a student who loved reading books,” said Betal. “One day, he lost his favorite book.”

He searched everywhere but could not find it.

Another student had found the book but decided to keep it.

Later, the teacher asked, “Has anyone found a lost book?”

The second student felt guilty.

He slowly stood up and returned the book.

The teacher smiled and said, “You made a mistake, but you chose to correct it.”

The student felt relieved.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what was important here?”

Vikram replied, “Accepting a mistake and correcting it is true honesty.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Admitting mistakes is a sign of honesty.
